### Significance Tests

| Test | p-value | σ | Interpretation |
|------|---------|---|----------------|
| Sign test (median vs 1.0) | 0.628 | 0.48 | Median IS 1.0 — not different from balance |
| Overall binomial (50/50) | 0.469 | 0.08 | Consistent with perfect 50/50 balance |
| Bootstrap balance excess (1,000 shuffles) | <0.001 | 6.36σ | Highly significant excess of balanced superclusters |
| Bootstrap balance excess (10,000 shuffles) | <0.0001 | >3.72σ | 0/10,000 random shuffles exceeded observed |
| Direct sigma from random mean | — | **4.29σ** | (347−305.4)/9.7 |
| Wilcoxon signed rank | <0.0001 | 6.64σ | Distribution significantly centered on 1.0 |

**Key result: In 10,000 random shuffles the maximum balanced
superclusters ever achieved was 342. The real universe shows 347.
Zero random universes exceeded the observed balance.**

