### Physical Threshold Test

To test whether extreme states preferentially co-occur, we used
physical thresholds instead of median split:
- Genuinely disturbed: D_COMB > 0.5
- Genuinely relaxed: D_COMB < 0.1
- Middle ground: 0.1 – 0.5

**Full eROSITA sample distribution:**

| Population | Count | Fraction |
|-----------|-------|---------|
| Genuinely disturbed (D_COMB > 0.5) | 2,275 | 18.6% |
| Middle ground (0.1–0.5) | 5,803 | 47.4% |
| Genuinely relaxed (D_COMB < 0.1) | 4,169 | 34.0% |

**Co-occurrence test:**
- Superclusters with genuine disturbed: 644
- Of those, also having genuine relaxed: 373 (57.9%)
- Random expectation: 404.4 ± 12.7
- Result: p=0.994 — observed BELOW random at 2.52σ

**Interpretation:** Genuinely violent mergers and pristine cool cores
do NOT preferentially co-occur within superclusters. The balance signal
from the median split reflects uniform sampling of the morphology
distribution — not pairing of extremes.

Most clusters in any supercluster occupy the middle ground (47.4%) —
neither violently merging nor pristine cool cores. The balance we
detect is in how the full morphology spectrum is distributed across
superclusters, not in the pairing of extremes.

