## Caveats

- D_COMB morphology not mass-matched per supercluster — mass
  distribution within superclusters not controlled
- eROSITA western hemisphere only — full sky test requires future data
- Mean ratio (1.343) pulled by outliers — median (1.000) is the
  robust statistic
- Median split by construction gives 50/50 globally — the significance
  is in the uniformity of distribution across superclusters not the
  overall ratio
- Requires independent confirmation with PSZ2 or ACT morphology
- Redshift evolution confirms known science — not a new discovery
- Physical threshold test shows extremes don't pair — balance is
  population-level not pairwise

